  "summary": "Explore 2025 population size and density, plus estimated population change since 2001, across B.C.'s regional districts.",
  "sourceNote": "The original Environmental Reporting BC indicator and repository reported 1986–2017. This project applies the same regional population and density method to the newer open BC Stats Sub-Provincial Population Estimates table. The current table provides a consistent regional-district series from 2001–2025, so the change map uses that period. Geometry is shared with the municipal solid waste project through one reusable census-division layer.",
  "details": [
    "Click or tap a regional district for its 2025 population estimate, land area, density, and change from 2001.",
    "Population estimates describe where people live; they do not directly measure environmental pressure or impact.",
    "The regional district series includes Stikine and Northern Rockies as census divisions."
